@flexiarg problems/facade-instead-of-validated-efe-model
@title Problem node: a facade in place of a validated EFE model
@keywords problem-node, facade, R5-spine, EFE, worked-around-fundamentals
@audience futon stack operators, library authors
@tone plain
@style pattern
@why ruling authority: futon2 holes labs wm-contract EPIC-run-era.md, The R5-spine reckoning (Joe, 2026-09-05); no library pattern grounds this node
@how no mechanism claimed at problem grain; the ruling's found mechanism is P-validated-R5.md parked behind its operator-acceptance gate

! conclusion: This is a problem-stating node: effort to bake in the fundamentals was ignored or worked around, leaving yet another facade instead of a validated EFE model, so the machine does not centre cascades, policy, and G as its core units.

  + context: Minted by library-loop row L5 from EPIC-run-era.md; it exists so @why edges from facade-detection patterns have a problem node to land on.

  + IF:
    Days of work and deep dives into a relationship (cascades, policy, G) fail to centre it in the machine built on it.

  + HOWEVER:
    The problem, per the ruling (Joe, verbatim, 2026-09-05): "how is it possible that after days of work, and many deep dives into the relationship between cascades and policy and G, the machine does not centre those as its core units? ... This is worse than Q not being defined. It seems to me that my effort to get the fundamentals baked in has been either ignored or worked around, with yet another façade in place instead of a validated EFE model based on the topics we actually discussed. For all I KNOW the code was built but not wired again. ... Noting also that all work that doesn't build appropriately on the fundamentals will have to be redone or discarded." The found mechanism: P-validated-R5.md held exactly this program and sat behind its operator-acceptance gate, which became the parking brake. (source: futon2 holes labs wm-contract EPIC-run-era.md, The R5-spine reckoning, 2026-09-05)

  + THEN:
    Treat this node as the landing point for @why edges from patterns that answer facade-building; solving it is the spine program's job, not this node's.

  + BECAUSE:
    A facade passes every individually-validated check while invalidating the work it fronts; all non-spine work on top of it is redo or discard.
    + evidence: futon2 holes labs wm-contract EPIC-run-era.md, "## The R5-spine reckoning (Joe, 2026-09-05) — and the gate that parked it".
